  "worked_solution": "Let $A$ denote the area under the curve $y=C(t)$ over $[0,15].$ In this case, we have $n=4$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is approximated as \n\n$$\nA\u2248C(3)\u0394{t}_{1}+C(7)\u0394{t}_{2}+C(12)\u0394{t}_{3}+C(15)\u0394{t}_{4},\n$$\n\nwhere each $\u0394{t}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $t$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\u0394{t}_{i}={t}_{i}-{t}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $\u0394t$'s.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $3$ | $7$ | $12$ | $15$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\u0394t$ | $-$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n| $C(t)$ | $-$ | $4$ | $3$ | $5$ | $2$ |\n\nWe plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u22484\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 4+5\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12+12+25+6 \\\\  & =55.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total number of customers served over a period of $15$ minutes. So, the total number of customers is approximately\n$55.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
